<title>USA: Favorable harvest weather seen for U.S. HRW wheat.</title>
<headline>Favorable harvest weather seen for U.S. HRW wheat.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hard red winter harvest should advance this week as forecasts call for hot, dry weather for much of Kansas and Oklahoma until next week, meteorologists said.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be decent harvest weather,&quot; said Fred Gesser, Weather Express Inc meteorologist.</p>
<p>Forecasts call for highs in the 90s to low 100 degrees Fahrenheit Tuesday and Wednesday, with readings slipping to the mid-80s and low 90s Thursday through Friday.</p>
<p>Scattered showers may occur in Oklahoma and Texas Friday, but otherwise the next significant rain event should be July 8 and 9, meteorologists said.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think there will be much (rain) in Kansas Friday,&quot; said Joel Burgio, meteorologist with Weather Services Corp.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
